<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deskaheh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1873">1873</a>–<a href="/years/1925">1925</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Levi General</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deskaheh, born Levi General, was a Cayuga chief and speaker of the traditional council of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-nations-of-the-grand-river">Six Nations of the Grand River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>. In 1923 he travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> on a Haudenosaunee passport to ask the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> to recognise the Six Nations as a sovereign people. The appeal failed, and in 1924 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> replaced the traditional council with an elected band council. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> State in 1925.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/deskaheh.jpg" alt="Deskaheh" width="279" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Graphic (an illustrated weekly newspaper) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deskaheh_photo.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
